[
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "hook",
    "language": "en",
    "text": "We assigned the task by opportunity cost. Now attach a price. Raising the price does not always raise the cash in the till. It depends how many buyers walk away — the elasticity of demand.",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\en\\hook.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "define",
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Price elasticity of demand is the percent change in quantity demanded divided by the percent change in price. If that ratio is above one, demand is elastic.",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\en\\define.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "example",
    "language": "en",
    "text": "A small rise in the rice price barely cuts bowls sold, so revenue can rise. The same rise on a snack people can skip empties the queue and can cut revenue.",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\en\\example.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "formula",
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Elasticity is not the slope of the curve. It is how much quantity moves when price moves by one percent. Units cancel. The ratio stays.",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\en\\formula.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "split",
    "language": "en",
    "text": "If quantity jumps more than price, demand is elastic and a higher price can shrink revenue. If quantity barely moves, a higher price can raise revenue.",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\en\\split.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "mtr",
    "language": "en",
    "text": "A ten percent fare rise cuts rides by three percent. |Ed| is 0.3. Demand here is inelastic, so revenue rises even as some riders leave.",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\en\\mtr.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "drivers",
    "language": "en",
    "text": "More substitutes, a larger share of income, and a longer month all raise elasticity. A morning commute with one line is less elastic than a weekend lunch.",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\en\\drivers.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "use",
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Write a guess for |Ed|. If it is below one, revenue may rise. Still ask who remains: students, tourists, or people with no other line.",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\en\\use.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "cut",
    "language": "en",
    "text": "One is the hinge. Above it, quantity dominates the revenue story. Below it, price does. Do not quote a slope and call it elasticity.",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\en\\cut.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "takeaway",
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Many substitutes mean elastic demand. A price rise then loses quantity faster than it gains on each unit. Next sitting asks what one price does to buyers and sellers together — surplus, shortage, and a price that clears.",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\en\\takeaway.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "hook",
    "language": "zh_cn",
    "text": "任务已按机会成本分好。现在标上价格。涨价并不总是让抽屉里的现金变多。要看有多少买家走开——也就是需求弹性。",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\zh_cn\\hook.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "define",
    "language": "zh_cn",
    "text": "需求价格弹性是需求量的百分比变化除以价格的百分比变化。若这个比值大于一，需求就是有弹性的。",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\zh_cn\\define.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "example",
    "language": "zh_cn",
    "text": "米饭小幅涨价，卖掉的份数几乎不减，收入可能上升。同样涨在可放弃的宵夜上，队伍会散，收入可能下降。",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\zh_cn\\example.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "formula",
    "language": "zh_cn",
    "text": "弹性不是曲线的斜率。它是价格变动百分之一时，数量变动多少。单位消掉。比值留下。",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\zh_cn\\formula.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "split",
    "language": "zh_cn",
    "text": "若数量跳得比价格多，需求有弹性，提价可能减少收入。若数量几乎不动，提价可能增加收入。",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\zh_cn\\split.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "mtr",
    "language": "zh_cn",
    "text": "票价升百分之十，乘次降百分之三。|Ed|是0.3。这里需求缺乏弹性，所以即使有人离开，收入仍上升。",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\zh_cn\\mtr.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "drivers",
    "language": "zh_cn",
    "text": "替代越多、占收入越大、可调整的时间越长，弹性越大。只有一条线的早高峰，比周末午餐更缺乏弹性。",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\zh_cn\\drivers.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "use",
    "language": "zh_cn",
    "text": "先写下|Ed|的猜测。若小于一，收入可能上升。仍要问留下的是谁：学生、游客，还是没有其他线路的人。",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\zh_cn\\use.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "cut",
    "language": "zh_cn",
    "text": "一是铰链。高于一，数量主导收入故事。低于一，价格主导。不要引用斜率却把它叫做弹性。",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\zh_cn\\cut.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "takeaway",
    "language": "zh_cn",
    "text": "替代品多，需求就有弹性。这时涨价，数量掉得比每件多收的钱更快。下一单元问一个价格如何同时作用于买卖双方——过剩、短缺，以及出清的价格。",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\zh_cn\\takeaway.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "hook",
    "language": "zh_hk",
    "text": "任務已按機會成本分好。現在標上價格。漲價並不總是讓抽屜裏的現金變多。要看有多少買家走開——也就是需求彈性。",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\zh_hk\\hook.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "ECON-EL-01",
    "beat_id": "define",
    "language": "zh_hk",
    "text": "需求價格彈性是需求量的百分比變化除以價格的百分比變化。若這個比值大於一，需求就是有彈性的。",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\ECON-EL-01\\audio\\zh_hk\\define.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
